WEBVTT

00:33.740 --> 00:35.920
For the first time in the 
history of the empire...

00:36.750 --> 00:40.850
a woman will be awarded the 
Order of the Imperial Rose.

00:46.510 --> 00:48.800
What is it? Has something happened?

00:57.340 --> 00:58.170
What?

01:03.760 --> 01:05.200
Elise?

01:05.500 --> 01:06.760
Are you all right?

01:06.760 --> 01:10.100
Yes. Just a little startled, that's all.

01:10.100 --> 01:12.710
I-I'm so sorry.

01:13.040 --> 01:16.800
With the rain, I couldn't 
see in front of us.

01:17.960 --> 01:19.140
Oh, no!

02:56.610 --> 02:58.100
The bone is broken.

02:58.100 --> 03:00.020
Please wait here for a moment.

03:02.460 --> 03:05.040
This is a problem. I don't have a splint.

03:09.530 --> 03:11.370
Might you be able to use this?

03:12.900 --> 03:16.040
I believe so, but...

03:16.270 --> 03:20.330
Are you worried for me
because I'll get wet in the rain?

03:20.330 --> 03:22.050
This is nothing.

03:22.640 --> 03:27.550
Not compared to your conducting an 
examination despite the mud.

03:27.840 --> 03:31.800
Thank you. Then, I will use it.

03:31.800 --> 03:32.910
I'll help.

03:32.910 --> 03:33.820
What?

03:33.820 --> 03:37.320
We have to make sure that his 
leg can't move, correct?

03:37.320 --> 03:39.100
Yes, that's right.

03:39.100 --> 03:41.350
Please hold it steady, just like that.

03:43.820 --> 03:46.290
Please bear with it just a little longer.

03:46.290 --> 03:48.410
Once it's stabilized, 
the pain should lessen.

03:56.660 --> 03:58.450
What is this gentleman's name?

03:58.450 --> 03:59.840
It's Daniel.

04:01.570 --> 04:04.200
Everything is all right, Mister Daniel.

04:06.510 --> 04:08.080
Y-Yes, miss.

04:32.700 --> 04:35.860
Fortunately, it doesn't seem 
to be a compound fracture.

04:35.860 --> 04:37.510
Thank you.

04:37.510 --> 04:41.010
I'll make arrangements for our 
doctor to visit tomorrow.

04:41.370 --> 04:42.820
Please do.

04:45.590 --> 04:47.630
I'm sorry! I've been so inconsiderate!

04:47.630 --> 04:49.430
You're soaking wet, aren't you?

04:49.430 --> 04:51.770
I'll show you to the bathroom right away.

04:51.770 --> 04:56.660
N-No. I'm thankful for your kindness, 
but I'll be leaving now.

04:57.050 --> 04:58.630
Leaving?

05:06.250 --> 05:08.020
In this?

05:11.430 --> 05:13.850
Why don't you stay here for tonight?

05:13.850 --> 05:14.910
What?

05:15.330 --> 05:18.920
I can't send you in a carriage, 
and it's already quite late.

05:19.300 --> 05:22.510
But... wouldn't I be imposing?

05:23.200 --> 05:24.490
Don't worry.

05:24.490 --> 05:26.150
Because the storm is so bad,

05:26.150 --> 05:28.430
my older brother said he'd be 
staying over at work.

05:28.430 --> 05:30.890
My father won't be home tonight either.

05:39.430 --> 05:43.550
<i>I never imagined I'd be staying the 
night in the Child family estate.</i>

05:45.120 --> 05:49.630
<i>Our houses don't get along, so the 
idea never even occurred to me.</i>

05:53.570 --> 05:54.640
Yes?

05:56.610 --> 05:58.830
Was the water hot enough?

05:59.200 --> 06:02.360
Yes! I'm quite warmed up now!

06:02.360 --> 06:03.380
I'm glad to hear that.

06:05.530 --> 06:06.660
Please, have some.

06:06.660 --> 06:08.140
Thank you.

06:15.030 --> 06:18.220
My clothes are a little 
large for you, aren't they?

06:20.400 --> 06:22.050
Yes, I suppose they are.

06:24.490 --> 06:25.950
This is delicious!

06:25.950 --> 06:28.370
It has ginger in it, doesn't it?

06:28.370 --> 06:29.130
Yes.

06:29.800 --> 06:32.990
You remember when I had caught a cold?

06:32.990 --> 06:34.210
Yes.

06:34.580 --> 06:37.700
After that, I started drinking it often.

06:38.320 --> 06:43.570
It's warming, and it improves blood flow 
which increases the body's immunity.

06:44.850 --> 06:47.960
You know about immunity?

06:47.960 --> 06:48.730
What?

06:49.370 --> 06:52.940
Could it be that you're studying medicine?

06:52.940 --> 06:57.720
Earlier, when you were helping me, 
your execution was very good, too.

07:02.620 --> 07:07.240
I tried studying just a little 
because I was jealous of you.

07:09.240 --> 07:11.500
Of me?

07:13.630 --> 07:17.750
Right now, everyone is 
watching Elise de Clorence.

07:18.460 --> 07:20.880
Your every move is reported on.

07:20.880 --> 07:23.450
There are even magazines with 
special collections about you.

07:23.830 --> 07:25.240
What?

07:26.310 --> 07:29.340
Receiving the Order of the
Imperial Rose is incredible.

07:29.750 --> 07:31.070
Oh, but...

07:31.070 --> 07:33.130
There's no need to be humble.

07:33.130 --> 07:35.160
It's a tremendous honor.

07:35.160 --> 07:37.990
You're going to be awarded an 
honorary knighthood, aren't you?

07:37.990 --> 07:39.060
Yes.

07:42.340 --> 07:47.030
Right now, you're walking a precipitous 
path that no one else has managed.

07:48.100 --> 07:53.430
And where you have walked, so many new 
hopes spring up in your footsteps.

07:53.430 --> 07:56.800
I was jealous of you for 
being able to do that.

07:57.530 --> 08:00.090
That's why I tried imitating you.

08:00.090 --> 08:06.530
If I study medicine, perhaps I'll be able 
to become like you. It's childish logic.

08:06.870 --> 08:10.800
Of course, I know that 
it won't be that simple.

08:11.430 --> 08:12.540
But...

08:14.090 --> 08:16.850
I simply couldn't sit still and do nothing.

08:18.080 --> 08:20.340
And so, the official announcement 
of their engagement...

08:21.430 --> 08:27.150
will wait until after Lady 
Clorence has come of age.

08:30.840 --> 08:34.980
Ever since that day, my heart has been...

08:37.910 --> 08:39.760
just like this storm.

08:43.470 --> 08:44.990
<i>I knew it.</i>

08:45.820 --> 08:50.720
<i>Juliane's heart was broken by 
that engagement announcement.</i>

08:52.070 --> 08:55.660
<i>The Child family is part of the nobles' 
faction, so they and the crown prince...</i>

08:55.660 --> 08:57.100
<i>are enemies.</i>

09:01.670 --> 09:04.040
<i>Unless some sort of miracle occurs,</i>

09:04.040 --> 09:06.790
<i>Lady Juliane and the crown 
prince will never...</i>

09:10.990 --> 09:12.110
Juliane.

09:19.610 --> 09:24.160
Elise, you have so many 
truly wonderful things...

09:26.130 --> 09:29.360
while I have nothing.

09:30.620 --> 09:33.870
I-I've said too much.

09:33.870 --> 09:36.640
I'll have a bedroom readied 
for you right away.

09:37.500 --> 09:40.710
Please, stay warm and sleep well, Elise.

09:40.710 --> 09:41.630
I will,

09:41.980 --> 09:43.980
since you insist.

09:48.180 --> 09:52.440
<i>I didn't intend to say 
any of that. So, why...</i>

09:54.560 --> 09:57.210
Elise is quite an unusual person.

10:04.970 --> 10:06.900
Thirty-nine degrees.

10:07.270 --> 10:08.800
That's a high fever.

10:10.450 --> 10:13.420
I'm truly so very sorry.

10:14.030 --> 10:16.010
This is nothing to apologize for.

10:16.430 --> 10:20.630
And Doctor Kyle is here today. 
I'll have him examine you, too.

10:21.150 --> 10:22.230
Yes.

10:22.670 --> 10:24.980
Excuse me, my lady.

10:25.530 --> 10:27.860
Lord Albert has returned.

10:27.860 --> 10:30.560
He said he would be visiting 
your rooms right away.

10:32.500 --> 10:33.930
All right.

10:37.950 --> 10:40.960
Um, Juliane...

10:41.500 --> 10:44.580
I'll have someone bring you some soup.

10:44.580 --> 10:48.140
All you need to do is focus
on getting well soon.

10:51.960 --> 10:55.950
Why is Elise de Clorence 
here at our residence?

10:55.950 --> 10:59.980
The carriage I was riding 
in nearly ran Elise down.

10:59.980 --> 11:01.830
What? What happened after that?

11:01.830 --> 11:04.200
She was unhurt.

11:05.970 --> 11:07.160
I see.

11:07.160 --> 11:11.290
If the Child family had injured the 
daughter of the House of Clorence,

11:11.290 --> 11:12.730
it would be a huge problem.

11:13.020 --> 11:15.160
However, the coachman suffered a broken leg,

11:15.160 --> 11:17.870
and Elise provided emergency 
medical treatment.

11:17.870 --> 11:20.980
And because she was drenched in rain 
while doing that, she's caught a cold.

11:20.980 --> 11:24.140
I see. I understand the situation now.

11:24.140 --> 11:27.500
However, you must have her 
leave as soon as possible.

11:27.500 --> 11:30.950
That will depend upon Elise's condition.

11:30.950 --> 11:35.010
If we send her home while she's feeling 
unwell and something happens, it won't be good.

11:35.370 --> 11:39.560
You aren't going to tell me that 
you've become friends, are you?

11:43.030 --> 11:44.420
You're not suited to each other.

11:44.420 --> 11:45.080
What?

11:45.340 --> 11:49.590
Not someone like you, who hates to 
lose, and that unreliable young lady.

11:57.840 --> 11:59.420
Unreliable?

12:00.370 --> 12:03.150
<i>So, that's how my older brother sees her?</i>

12:16.810 --> 12:20.900
This seems the be the beginning of a cold. 
I'll prescribe some medicine.

12:20.900 --> 12:23.980
Your fever should go down quite soon.

12:23.980 --> 12:25.550
Thank you.

12:25.550 --> 12:29.310
Not at all. Please, take 
good care of yourself.

12:29.610 --> 12:32.070
How is Mister Daniel?

12:32.070 --> 12:34.520
Oh, he's just fine.

12:34.520 --> 12:37.230
A full recovery will
probably take four weeks.

12:37.230 --> 12:40.680
Or perhaps three weeks, at the quickest.

12:40.680 --> 12:43.940
You treatment was well done. 
It was a great help.

12:43.940 --> 12:45.290
I'm so glad.

12:45.290 --> 12:47.470
It's thanks to you, Lady Clorence.

12:47.470 --> 12:50.700
Oh, no. Juliane helped 
with the treatment, too.

12:51.200 --> 12:52.600
Lady Juliane helped, too?

12:52.600 --> 12:57.240
There's no need for such surprise. 
I steadied the splint, that's all.

12:57.240 --> 12:58.440
I see.

13:04.710 --> 13:09.770
<i>To think that Lady Juliane would smile at 
someone from the House of Clorence like that.</i>

13:11.200 --> 13:16.400
<i>It might be that this lady will change 
more than just the world of medicine.</i>

13:23.230 --> 13:26.370
I'm so sorry. You shouldn't 
have to do this for me.

13:26.370 --> 13:29.230
But it feels awful to be 
covered in sweat, doesn't it?

13:29.600 --> 13:31.590
May I tie your hair back for you?

13:31.590 --> 13:35.750
What? Yes. Thank you.

13:43.920 --> 13:47.390
Amazing. You're very deft at this, Juliane.

13:47.750 --> 13:51.470
Do you think so? Anyone can 
manage this much, can't they?

13:53.630 --> 13:55.770
Could it be that you can't?

13:57.730 --> 13:58.780
That's right.

14:00.080 --> 14:04.070
When you can successfully perform 
all those difficult surgeries?

14:04.070 --> 14:05.270
That's unexpected.

14:07.250 --> 14:08.270
All done.

14:12.660 --> 14:15.500
Juliane, you're such a kind person.

14:15.500 --> 14:16.280
What?

14:16.560 --> 14:19.290
When I'm with you, I feel at ease 
from the bottom of my heart.

14:22.290 --> 14:25.240
Juliane? Your face has turned red.

14:25.240 --> 14:27.580
Have you caught my cold?

14:27.580 --> 14:29.040
Th-That's not it!

14:29.350 --> 14:33.260
It's because I've never 
been told I'm kind before.

14:33.260 --> 14:34.890
Really?

14:35.550 --> 14:39.570
Ever since I was little, I've run 
around, following my brother.

14:39.570 --> 14:42.670
When someone's done something 
wrong or something I can't accept

14:42.670 --> 14:46.060
regardless of who it might be, I tell them 
about it. That's just my personality.

14:46.560 --> 14:51.710
Just a little while ago, my older 
brother told me that I hate to lose.

14:51.710 --> 14:53.220
I'm the same way.

14:53.220 --> 14:57.340
I get stubborn and say and 
do things I shouldn't.

14:57.690 --> 14:59.240
I already know that.

14:59.240 --> 14:59.960
What?

15:00.650 --> 15:03.830
After all, the old you was 
completely unbelievable.

15:08.190 --> 15:11.380
Well, if you'll excuse me,
 I'll take my leave.

15:15.350 --> 15:17.260
Why, whatever happened?

15:17.260 --> 15:20.610
Tripping over nothing in 
such an unsightly manner...

15:45.690 --> 15:49.390
Oh, my. How terribly unbecoming of a lady!

15:54.960 --> 15:58.530
I've suffered through so 
much childish harassment.

15:58.530 --> 16:01.890
I hated you from the bottom of my heart.

16:05.650 --> 16:07.530
But it's different now.

16:07.530 --> 16:08.320
What?

16:08.810 --> 16:10.800
I respect you very much.

16:24.300 --> 16:26.170
The breeze feels so nice.

16:26.970 --> 16:28.420
Say, Elise?

16:28.420 --> 16:32.180
When you're feeling better, what would 
you think of fulfilling that promise?

16:41.390 --> 16:42.690
Today,

16:43.130 --> 16:46.020
I would like to discuss Elise de Clorence,

16:46.020 --> 16:49.620
who has garnered tremendous 
support from the people.

16:50.940 --> 16:57.130
She is currently someone whom Laurage, 
no, all of the empire is watching.

16:57.130 --> 17:01.690
And though it isn't official, she was 
announced as the crown princess, wasn't she?

17:03.410 --> 17:08.270
Perhaps because of that, the crown 
prince's approval rating has increased.

17:09.360 --> 17:11.710
That is exactly the problem.

17:11.710 --> 17:16.710
Until now, in the citizens' approval ratings 
of the crown prince and our third prince,

17:16.710 --> 17:20.170
his approval rating was
much lower than Prince Mikhail's.

17:20.170 --> 17:21.220
Indeed.

17:21.580 --> 17:27.220
The people don't want Crown Prince 
Linden. They want Prince Mikhail.

17:27.730 --> 17:30.480
But if current conditions continue,

17:30.480 --> 17:34.000
the nobles' faction may find 
itself in a difficult position.

17:34.000 --> 17:36.700
More importantly, if we are defeated

17:36.700 --> 17:39.820
and Linden de Romanoff 
ascends the imperial throne,

17:39.820 --> 17:43.950
it's certain that he won't simply let us be.

17:44.690 --> 17:46.560
Not after the events of that day.

17:50.380 --> 17:52.570
He will never forgive us.

18:06.520 --> 18:09.690
At least three will die.

18:09.690 --> 18:12.100
My mother, my uncle...

18:12.580 --> 18:14.110
and me.

18:24.650 --> 18:25.810
This is delicious!

18:26.410 --> 18:29.290
Juliane, you can make sweets, too?

18:29.290 --> 18:31.600
I'm glad it suits your taste.

18:31.600 --> 18:35.130
There's plenty here, so feel free
 to take some home with you.

18:38.270 --> 18:39.290
Juliane.

18:39.290 --> 18:40.040
What is it?

18:40.410 --> 18:42.380
You said something earlier...

18:42.380 --> 18:48.570
that I have many wonderful things, 
while you have nothing.

18:49.600 --> 18:50.720
Yes.

18:50.720 --> 18:52.960
I understand that feeling.

18:54.360 --> 18:56.590
Because I didn't have anything either.

18:57.070 --> 18:59.320
But that isn't... You're...

19:01.140 --> 19:02.850
I had nothing.

19:04.250 --> 19:06.740
If I had anything, it was 
only loneliness and regrets.

19:07.390 --> 19:10.830
But in spite of— no, because of that...

19:11.590 --> 19:16.100
I devoted everything I had to continuing 
to do whatever I was able to do.

19:24.710 --> 19:28.270
I didn't know you at all, 
and I selfishly assumed...

19:28.760 --> 19:29.910
I'm sorry.

19:32.930 --> 19:36.530
It's the people with nothing 
who can become the strongest.

19:38.020 --> 19:41.820
I'm saying this from experience, 
so there's no mistake.

19:44.890 --> 19:46.530
What does that even mean?

19:46.810 --> 19:48.840
I realize that you're trying to comfort me,

19:48.840 --> 19:53.030
but you're practically confirming 
the fact that I have nothing.

19:53.030 --> 19:56.270
What? No, I... That isn't what I meant!

19:58.510 --> 20:00.060
You seem a little too flustered.

20:00.620 --> 20:02.540
W-Well, it's just...

20:02.540 --> 20:04.760
Oh, I'm so sorry!

20:04.760 --> 20:07.010
You lent me these clothes...

20:07.010 --> 20:08.940
and I've gotten them dirty.

20:10.320 --> 20:13.940
Oh! Of course I'll clean them properly 
before I return them to you.

20:14.530 --> 20:17.250
You fulfilled your promise 
to have tea with me,

20:17.250 --> 20:20.060
and you've already made me another promise.

20:22.500 --> 20:24.070
Yes, I have.

20:32.590 --> 20:34.090
Say, Elise?

20:34.440 --> 20:35.180
Yes?

20:35.810 --> 20:39.850
When your big moment comes, 
as it surely will,

20:39.850 --> 20:41.990
I'll do your hair for you.

20:52.370 --> 20:53.350
Elise!

20:53.730 --> 20:57.470
I heard from the messenger! You've 
been at the estate of the Child family?

20:57.470 --> 20:58.910
Y-Yes.

20:58.910 --> 21:00.600
You stayed the night there?

21:00.600 --> 21:03.990
Did anything bad happen? 
Did they frighten you?

21:03.990 --> 21:08.120
Not in the least. They treated me very well.

21:08.120 --> 21:10.430
Well?! Well, you say?

21:10.430 --> 21:12.150
Treated well by the Child family?

21:12.150 --> 21:14.110
I heard that you had a fever.

21:15.610 --> 21:17.890
But I'm all right now.

21:17.890 --> 21:19.090
Truly?

21:19.090 --> 21:23.880
Truly! Juliane looked after me, 
so I'm completely well now.

21:24.220 --> 21:27.230
Lady Juliane? That can't be.

21:28.310 --> 21:30.190
What do you mean?

21:30.190 --> 21:32.880
W-Well, we are talking about 
the House of Child here.

21:32.880 --> 21:35.960
Yes, we are. That House of Child.

21:35.960 --> 21:39.520
But Juliane and I are friends.

21:42.540 --> 21:44.310
Oh, that's right!

21:44.310 --> 21:45.170
Here it is.

21:45.900 --> 21:47.110
What is it?

21:49.310 --> 21:50.630
Just a little parting gift.

21:51.470 --> 21:54.840
Juliane made them herself! 
She's amazing, isn't she?

22:06.300 --> 22:10.050
After the Storm
